WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:21.930
My adrenaline's always flowin'

2
00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:28.510
So it feels like I'll overheat

3
00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:32.850
Even if I explode and turn to ashes

4
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:39.600
I'll probably still be laughing
Just like this

5
00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:45.120
Blowing past the town
To the ends of the world

6
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:50.600
Let's burn rubber
And die together like lovers

7
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:55.430
Let's cut loose
Until we reach our limit

8
00:00:56.210 --> 00:01:00.470
So we can reach the horizon

9
00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.940
Crash! Into the rolling morning

10
00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:08.580
Flash!
I'm in the coolest driver's high

11
00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:13.920
Toward the finish line

12
00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:43.230
Tom is two years old.

13
00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:47.520
Uncle Ben says,
"Tom you are very smart."

14
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.920
When this is translated
into English...

15
00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:54.210
Tom is two years old.

16
00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:58.360
Uncle Ben says,
"You are very clever, Tom!"

17
00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:03.660
Hey, why is Sakurada teaching
from such an easy section?

18
00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:06.200
Maybe he is afraid that
a certain someone might point out...

19
00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.840
...his mistakes if he gives us
difficult material.

20
00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:09.910
Teacher!

21
00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:15.510
Your translation
was a little wrong.

22
00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:23.150
The word "clever" implies
"sneaky" and "sly."

23
00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:27.760
Do you think it's appropriate to use
such a word for a two-year-old?

24
00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:31.160
Here we go again!

25
00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:37.120
In this case, Americans would use
the word "smart." "You are smart!"

26
00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:40.070
You would know at least that much
if you watched foreign movies and stuff.

27
00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.580
Faculty Room

28
00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:46.810
What about Americans?!

29
00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.510
Don't make fun of me!

30
00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:50.450
Mr. Sakurada. Calm down!

31
00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:52.940
I... I wanted to go abroad...

32
00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:55.350
...and learn English
in a native environment!

33
00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:56.820
Whoa!

34
00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:59.920
But it wasn't that common
when I was young.

35
00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.890
If you have complaints, take them
to the Ministry of Education!

36
00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:06.120
He was attacked
by Kanzaki's class terrorism.

37
00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:08.320
Poor thing!
He's even talking differently.

38
00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:10.170
He usually addresses
himself as "me."

39
00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:13.540
Come on. How come
everyone is so flustered?

40
00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:15.440
She's just a kid.

41
00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:16.840
Isn't that right,
Miss Fuyutsuki?

42
00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:18.810
Don't talk to me!

43
00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:22.370
Fifth period is my turn.

44
00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:24.180
Oh, is that so?

45
00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.780
Science Lab 1

46
00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:26.780
So, in summary...

47
00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:30.150
...water is the combination
of hydrogen and oxygen.

48
00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.450
By performing electrolysis...

49
00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:35.550
...it could be separated
into hydrogen and oxygen.

50
00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:43.370
Kanzaki...

51
00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.260
Kikuchi!

52
00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:49.840
I don't care why you carry out
classroom terrorism.

53
00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:54.180
Hey, are you allowed to switch
seats without permission?

54
00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:57.310
But keep your
hands off of Onizuka!

55
00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:00.120
He is nothing like
any of the teachers you know.

56
00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:04.350
Hmmm.
Are you on his side, Kikuchi?

57
00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.650
Hard to believe, coming from someone
known as the master...

58
00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:10.160
...of bullying a homeroom
teacher in Class 2-4.

59
00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:13.560
You successfully drove
three teachers out of school!

60
00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:16.740
Don't worry.

61
00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:19.620
He's special for me, too.

62
00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:23.370
So I'll treat him special...

63
00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:29.150
Then let's do an experiment.

64
00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:31.060
Hey, Kikuchi.

65
00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:35.010
Doesn't your head feel clear
today... more than usual?

66
00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:35.710
What?

67
00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:40.080
It feels like this room
is full of oxygen.

68
00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:43.370
So... when you put a match closer
to the gas extracted in this manner...

69
00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:45.830
...you will find that this
is indeed hydrogen.

70
00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:54.140
Someone get a fire extinguisher!

71
00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:59.640
Ha ha ha... who in the world
would do such a bad thing?

72
00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:04.620
It's not funny. It's not funny!
It's worse than a joke!

73
00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:08.590
Look. Look. Look at my hair.
Look at my hair!

74
00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:13.030
I look like a chihuahua!
A chihuahua!

75
00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:15.570
How can you laugh?

76
00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:20.060
It's definitely a trick played
by someone in your class.

77
00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:23.690
I saw oxygen tanks
with open valves.

78
00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:25.500
It was intentional!

79
00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:26.970
Intentional!

80
00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:30.530
What... what... what are you
gonna do, Mr. Onizuka?!

81
00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:34.980
I... I was supposed to go to
a Nelton Party. Nelton. Nelton!

82
00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:37.640
It was going to be my 29th one.

83
00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:40.880
Besides, this time I paid extra
for a ticket...

84
00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:43.180
...to go to a Nelton Party with nurses.

85
00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:45.440
It was 25,000 yen.
25,000 yen!

86
00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:46.390
Hmm...

87
00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:50.300
Back home my parents have
been bugging me to get married!

88
00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.690
The party might have
been my only chance!

89
00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:55.830
Are you listening, Mr. Onizuka?

90
00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:58.250
Hey. Right there!
Don't laugh!

91
00:05:58.250 --> 00:05:58.740
Hmm...

92
00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:02.510
All right, all right.
I heard you.

93
00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:03.340
What?

94
00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:06.280
We already know who did it.

95
00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:12.760
I'll turn her into an obedient,
good girl with just one blow!

96
00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:17.390
Uh...

97
00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:19.860
Where are you going,
Mr. Onizuka?

98
00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:23.140
Uh... I was going to give
an extra-curricular class...

99
00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:24.530
In that outfit?

100
00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:27.290
Well... extra-curricular
in the subject of life.

101
00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:30.670
There is this kid whose tricks
are a little over the edge...

102
00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:33.400
It can't be Urumi Kanzaki,
can it?

103
00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:35.720
Huh? Well... sort of...

104
00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:37.530
Do you have proof?

105
00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:38.630
Proof?

106
00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:40.850
What?

107
00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:44.660
Have you forgotten
what I told you the other day?

108
00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:48.240
She is a specially treated student
certified by the Ministry of Education.

109
00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.550
She is a genius
with an IQ of 200!

110
00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:55.460
If anything should happen to her,
firing you wouldn't be enough!

111
00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:58.680
Do the other teachers
understand, too?

112
00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:00.400
With Urumi Kanzaki...

113
00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:04.540
...we expect all of you to handle her
carefully as if caring for a bruise!

114
00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:09.100
Kanzaki has been like that...

115
00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:12.860
...since before bullying of a homeroom
teacher began in our class.

116
00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:15.980
Yeah. She's been making a career
out of it more than we do.

117
00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:18.860
Besides the fact that she is
a specially treated student...

118
00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:23.400
...Kanzaki is kind of hard
to approach, even for us.

119
00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:27.630
That's right. She is kind of scary
to get involved with.

120
00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:31.430
When she stopped coming to school
I felt relieved, to be honest...

121
00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:33.430
Hmmm.

122
00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:40.530
I heard from Aizawa a long time ago
that she had a traumatic experience.

123
00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:42.360
Tora-uma? (tiger-horse)

124
00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:47.000
Is there such an animal?

125
00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:53.740
Is this guy imagining
something outrageous?

126
00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:54.820
He might be...

127
00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:59.280
So... Tora-uma...

128
00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:30.270
Oops?

129
00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:33.990
Huh? Where did she go?

130
00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:35.550
Teacher!

131
00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:36.590
Hmm!

132
00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:38.560
What are you doing?

133
00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:39.790
Uh...

134
00:08:40.030 --> 00:08:42.820
Did you need me?

135
00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:47.070
Hmm... I heard from Kikuchi
and his buddies.

136
00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:48.040
What?

137
00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:52.810
You... are holding in a huge
Tora-uma, aren't you?

138
00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:58.070
If that's the case, you should
have told me much earlier.

139
00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:01.610
I'm really good
at exterminating violent beasts!

140
00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:05.120
Teacher...
do you know what trauma is?

141
00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:07.330
Sure! Something like this, right?

142
00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:08.860
Eikichi Theatre
for Good Children

143
00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:12.300
A rare and violent beast, Tora-uma!

144
00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:11.800
Beast Of Trauma (Tora-Uma)
Temper: Violent

145
00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:14.800
Urumi is in a pinch!
Oh, no!

146
00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:14.800
Special Characteristic:
Eats Female Students

147
00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:16.230
Are you serious?

148
00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:17.710
Of course!

149
00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:22.210
Ah... ha ha ha.
Teacher, you're the best!

150
00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:23.900
Ah... ha ha ha...

151
00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:24.640
Hmm?

152
00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:29.110
Ramen

153
00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:28.390
Oh, now I understand.

154
00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:34.070
Tasty.

155
00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:36.180
Disgusting!

156
00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:37.630
Hah!

157
00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:40.970
Since the explanations by Kikuchi
and his buddies were a little strange...

158
00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:44.800
...I came to the conclusion that
a violent beast is living in your house...

159
00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:49.500
But... it would be a big problem
if such a beast settled in my house.

160
00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:50.870
Wouldn't it?

161
00:09:50.870 --> 00:09:53.560
You are... a nice person.

162
00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:57.310
Well, I'm just doing my job
as a teacher...

163
00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:00.280
But I happen to know...

164
00:10:00.650 --> 00:10:03.940
...that teachers in general don't hesitate
to abandon their students...

165
00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:05.250
...in a time of crisis.

166
00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:07.930
Huh? Hey, dummy!

167
00:10:07.930 --> 00:10:09.720
Why would I do that?

168
00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:12.320
Oh, really?

169
00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:13.090
What?

170
00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:15.160
Then I'll test it.

171
00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:17.130
One...

172
00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:19.130
...two... three!

173
00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:25.070
Ah! Dummy!

174
00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:26.980
It hit someone!

175
00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:27.990
Bingo!

176
00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:31.240
Umm... we're sorry. Are you O.K.?

177
00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:32.710
Oops!

178
00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:37.120
Punch Perm...
A gold button...

179
00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:39.550
Could... could he be...?

180
00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:41.160
Young boss.

181
00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:41.840
What?

182
00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:45.390
Who the hell are you?
Did you do this to our boss?

183
00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:47.260
Uh. No... Umm...

184
00:10:47.260 --> 00:10:52.620
Yes! I did! I was going
to clean up trash in the city!

185
00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:54.900
Hey, you stupid!
What are you saying!

186
00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:57.800
What are you gonna do?
Abandon me?

187
00:10:58.390 --> 00:10:59.740
Did you call us trash?
You brat!

188
00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:01.110
I can't believe it!

189
00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:03.910
Now, are you scared, young lady?

190
00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:09.280
You brat!

191
00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:11.880
Stupid!
Don't just stand there!

192
00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.780
Those bastards!
Wait!

193
00:11:28.460 --> 00:11:31.830
- Whoa!
- Help!

194
00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:41.800
- Did you see them?
- Shit! Where did they go?

195
00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:47.330
Phew.
We managed to get away.

196
00:11:48.110 --> 00:11:49.320
It was fun.

197
00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:50.570
In what sense?

198
00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:53.550
If we'd made even a minor mistake,
we would be...

199
00:11:53.550 --> 00:11:56.550
...at the bottom of Tokyo Bay
encased in concrete by now!

200
00:11:56.850 --> 00:11:59.030
Since we didn't make
a mistake, I don't care.

201
00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:02.690
Unbelievable!
I can't hang out with you.

202
00:12:04.460 --> 00:12:05.750
Where are you going?

203
00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:06.970
Going home.

204
00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:11.300
Those guys might be
hanging out in this area.

205
00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:14.600
If they find me, I might get killed...

206
00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:15.670
Why should I care?

207
00:12:18.150 --> 00:12:20.980
Oh... I see...

208
00:12:21.410 --> 00:12:23.550
Gosh... my life expectancy
has been shortened.

209
00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:25.870
Teacher...

210
00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:30.420
I'll kill myself!

211
00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:31.390
What?

212
00:12:31.990 --> 00:12:35.470
I'm gonna write a suicide note.

213
00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:38.430
- Hey. What are you doing, Kanzaki?

214
00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:42.360
A suicide note: I'm killing myself
because Mr. Onizuka hates me now.

215
00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:43.540
Crap!

216
00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:50.540
Whoa!
Don't kill yourself! If you do, I'll kill you!

217
00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:50.540
Farewell to everyone on the planet.

218
00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:53.760
Hello, everyone in heaven.

219
00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:56.220
Do you understand? Stay put!

220
00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:56.220
I'm joining you today as a new...

221
00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:01.120
Did I scare you?

222
00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:03.590
Of course you did!

223
00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:06.610
All right, all right.

224
00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:08.450
I won't abandon you.

225
00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:11.380
So don't ever play
this kind of joke on me again.

226
00:13:12.030 --> 00:13:14.370
It's not a joke.

227
00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:18.100
I was... half serious.

228
00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:19.010
What?

229
00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:22.310
Every now and then there are nights...

230
00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:25.280
...when I feel so lonely...
and depressed.

231
00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:29.970
I wonder why someone
like me was born into this world.

232
00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:34.030
I even wish I could vanish
from this world...

233
00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:39.650
...and pretend that I never existed...

234
00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:42.760
Stand up, Kanzaki.

235
00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:49.780
When I get negative thoughts like that,
it usually means I'm hungry.

236
00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:51.140
Seriously?

237
00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:54.540
Yeah. Also, we were
in the middle of eating ramen.

238
00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:57.570
Then I want to eat yakiniku!

239
00:13:57.570 --> 00:13:58.580
What?

240
00:13:58.580 --> 00:14:02.520
If I can't have it,
maybe I'll jump from here...

241
00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:04.020
Whoa...

242
00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:08.040
Wow... stop it!
Wait! Wait a second!

243
00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:12.720
Crap! Too many days 'til payday.

244
00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:15.600
Ah! Teacher,
there's some money at your feet!

245
00:14:16.060 --> 00:14:16.820
What?

246
00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:19.040
Oh, lucky!

247
00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:28.010
What?

248
00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:33.870
Kanzaki!

249
00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:38.330
Whoa!

250
00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:40.100
Whoa!

251
00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:48.500
Ouch. Hey, Kanzaki!
Are you all right?

252
00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:53.200
Whoa!

253
00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:55.280
Oh, this is a mannequin!

254
00:14:57.320 --> 00:15:00.510
Kanzaki! Oh, crap!

255
00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:04.490
Kanzaki! Wake up!

256
00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:09.320
She's dead!

257
00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:14.890
Murder By Butt Blow

258
00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:20.810
Chief Detective, what's the weapon?

259
00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:23.200
Hmm... probably one big butt blow.

260
00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:25.630
The entire mystery is solved!

261
00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:29.110
In the name of my grandpa...

262
00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:35.980
Please stop committing more crimes!

263
00:15:36.570 --> 00:15:40.040
"When we look back...
it is so admirable...

264
00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:43.750
...all the hard work
by our respectable teachers..."

265
00:15:44.180 --> 00:15:49.790
I happen to know that
teachers usually don't hesitate...

266
00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:51.590
...to abandon their students
in a time of crisis.

267
00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:55.060
COMING SOON TO THIS THEATRE

268
00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:58.500
Whoa! I don't have time
to turn this whole thing into a movie!

269
00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:01.390
Calm down!
Eikichi Onizuka. 22 years old!

270
00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:04.400
It's not that she's positively dead!

271
00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:09.480
If I rush her to a hospital...

272
00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:12.080
Hey.

273
00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:15.400
Hmm?
Hey, what are you doing?

274
00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:19.360
Ah! Wait!

275
00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:20.900
Wait!

276
00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:24.320
I look like a murder suspect
running away...

277
00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:27.490
...from the scene of the crime
after being noticed!

278
00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:30.200
Well, actually, it's pretty close to that...

279
00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:32.160
Crap, it's not even funny.

280
00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:33.200
Wait!

281
00:16:37.150 --> 00:16:40.740
Ah... I’ve got to do something
with this girl... this girl...

282
00:16:40.740 --> 00:16:42.330
...this corpse...

283
00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:43.750
Bury it.

284
00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:44.510
What?

285
00:16:45.090 --> 00:16:47.600
Bury it?
You mean this corpse?

286
00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:51.480
That's right.
Somewhere that's not conspicuous.

287
00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:55.460
What about a deep forest
near Mt. Fuji?

288
00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:58.600
- The body won't be easily found there.
- At the foot of Mt. Fuji.

289
00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:03.070
A deep forest near Mt. Fuji.

290
00:17:16.730 --> 00:17:19.150
What...
What am I doing?

291
00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:22.780
I look just like a murderer
on the Saturday Night Movie.

292
00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:26.680
Wake up! Wake up,
Eikichi Onizuka. 22 years old!

293
00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:28.510
You're a teacher!

294
00:17:28.510 --> 00:17:31.150
Do you think it's right for a teacher
to bury a student?

295
00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:34.830
That's right. Help her!
It may not be too late!

296
00:17:34.830 --> 00:17:37.100
But I've already brought her
to a forest. Hey...

297
00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:40.150
Ah! I know! CPR!

298
00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:45.700
Why didn't I think of it before?

299
00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:52.190
All right. I'm ready.

300
00:17:55.040 --> 00:18:00.060
Eikichi Onizuka. 22 years old.
A bachelor. Allow me to get going.

301
00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:06.630
Wah!

302
00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:12.800
I'll get you!

303
00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:16.840
Ah! I'm sorry.
Please cross over peacefully!

304
00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:22.310
Hey, could you stop treating me
like a dead person?

305
00:18:22.550 --> 00:18:23.860
What?

306
00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:28.720
Phew. No matter how it happened,
I'm glad you are alive.

307
00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:31.950
It's got to be the power of Mt. Fuji...
a spiritual, sacred mountain...

308
00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:34.180
Attempted murder
and abandonment of the corpse.

309
00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:40.130
Here, Kanzaki! Go ahead
and order whatever you want to eat!

310
00:18:40.130 --> 00:18:43.980
I want... a genie in a lamp.

311
00:18:43.980 --> 00:18:47.060
A genie?
Is there such a thing?

312
00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:48.530
Don't you know?

313
00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:51.000
You rub a lamp like this and say
something like, "Rah-ri-pap-pah."

314
00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:54.540
Then it appears and says,
"Aye-aye, Master."

315
00:18:54.540 --> 00:18:56.150
It's a fairy tale...

316
00:18:56.150 --> 00:19:00.020
...a malevolent deity who makes
whatever you wish for come true.

317
00:19:00.420 --> 00:19:02.220
You're not saying...
you want me to be...

318
00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:04.250
Yes, thank you.
All right?

319
00:19:04.510 --> 00:19:07.250
You must be joking!
Why should I...

320
00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:09.080
About 10 years in prison...

321
00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:12.010
...for attempted murder
and abandonment of a corpse...

322
00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:15.690
Like "Rah-ri-pap-pah!"
Genie!

323
00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:18.800
Come out
if you don't want to go to prison!

324
00:19:19.150 --> 00:19:22.640
Pah-pa-ra-pah!
Aye-aye, Master!

325
00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.960
Cool! So much fun!

326
00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:29.940
Hooray! Go, go. Speed away!

327
00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:34.410
Crap!
The motorcycle gangs from the area!

328
00:19:34.710 --> 00:19:37.450
Rah-ri-pap-pah! Genie!

329
00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:39.890
Go past them and speed away!

330
00:19:39.890 --> 00:19:40.590
What?

331
00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:42.930
Do you want to eat prison food?

332
00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:48.170
Ummm... Pah-pa-ra-pah!
As you wish, Master!

333
00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:51.300
Hold on tight!

334
00:19:52.340 --> 00:19:53.840
Move over, move over!

335
00:19:54.640 --> 00:19:57.310
Here comes a genie!

336
00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:02.810
Hey! Don't make light of Kofu Racing!

337
00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:05.720
Let's run away!

338
00:20:06.310 --> 00:20:08.850
Wait! We're gonna get you guys!

339
00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:11.750
Teacher!

340
00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:15.580
I've never had such a fun night.

341
00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:17.790
Oh, really?

342
00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:21.660
Really. I swear.
First time in my life!

343
00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:24.660
I'm gonna pee in my pants!

344
00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:25.980
Don't!

345
00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:29.520
Stop somewhere around here.

346
00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:36.470
Ah. Now I want to eat sweets
from Nagoya.

347
00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:40.140
That's right.
True sweets from Nagoya!

348
00:20:40.140 --> 00:20:41.210
Come on!

349
00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:42.750
10 years in prison!

350
00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:44.750
By tomorrow, please. O.K.?

351
00:20:45.940 --> 00:20:47.290
Aye-aye, Master.

352
00:20:50.910 --> 00:20:51.930
Kanzaki!

353
00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:56.500
Ah, I didn't know
Kikuchi's house was nearby.

354
00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:59.470
What did you do to Onizuka?

355
00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:01.940
You fell?

356
00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:06.280
Yeah.
What do you think he did, then?

357
00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:09.380
He jumped off to rescue you.

358
00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:15.380
Yup! Hmm... You know.

359
00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:18.290
He's that kind of a guy... Onizuka...

360
00:21:19.660 --> 00:21:21.520
That kind of a guy...

361
00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:25.610
What a brave guy to come back!

362
00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:27.230
We're gonna kill you this time!

363
00:21:27.230 --> 00:21:29.930
Don't make light of Kofu Racing!

364
00:21:47.090 --> 00:21:51.330
You and me, let's go away

365
00:21:51.530 --> 00:21:56.600
To look for new emotions today

366
00:21:56.700 --> 00:22:01.600
Together we can overcome

367
00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:07.540
Because I want to enjoy a new tomorrow

368
00:22:07.740 --> 00:22:11.950
Open your eyes and open the door

369
00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:17.150
The world in front of your eyes

370
00:22:17.880 --> 00:22:22.760
I want to go out
With my favorite sounds

371
00:22:23.090 --> 00:22:27.360
I will taste my childhood emotions

372
00:22:28.560 --> 00:22:38.170
I'm here to enjoy the sunlight

373
00:22:38.700 --> 00:22:48.180
I'm enjoying myself
More than in the past

374
00:22:48.310 --> 00:22:52.580
I want to see you, but I can't

375
00:22:52.780 --> 00:22:57.660
So I just embrace my love

376
00:22:57.890 --> 00:23:02.690
Even walking on a crowded street

377
00:23:02.960 --> 00:23:09.390
Your smile makes my head spin

378
00:23:19.930 --> 00:23:27.150
Next Episode

379
00:23:21.840 --> 00:23:23.250
Miss Fujimori.

380
00:23:23.750 --> 00:23:26.520
What? Is this teacher married?

381
00:23:26.520 --> 00:23:28.080
She's still not married.

382
00:23:28.590 --> 00:23:31.420
Because it's not tasty...

383
00:23:32.170 --> 00:23:34.430
...right, Miss Fujimori?
